g it's like being in a painting  it took dave six days to finish the race  and he only slept  a total of ten hours  it's that exhaustion he says that causes  you to lose your mind  your mind just starts imagining all  sorts i've went through  an avenue of trees and i thought i was  going through a disco party and every  time i approached somebody  they stopped talking and just looked at  me  but you can't stop  you've got to keep moving you think what  on earth is that coming towards me and  you know within two minutes you're  shivering you shouldn't have stopped  to look at something that's not there  i achieved what i wanted to achieve and  i finished it and i'm very grateful and  very lucky to have finished it  of all the races i've done it's one of  the most mentally challenging races out  there and it's probably the race that  commands the most respect  anybody who finishes that will well i  would certainly  they've got my admiration  oh yeah  a lot of people's reactions when we told  them were going to go basically to the  north pole or ride mountain bikes where  are you bringing ice tires you know  because most people think in the north  pole they're like okay it's gonna be  cold in full snow they don't really  realize that there's an arctic desert up  there  my name is daryn bearcloth i'm from  vancouver island british columbia and  i'm a professional mountain bike free  rider  free riding is all about picking your  own line and being free to interpret the  mountains in any way that you see fit  thinking about starting on the horizon  right there it'll be like a drop onto a  rock slab  the reason that we chose axel hybrid  island was because the lines were  massive it trumped anything that we ever  ridden before in terms of height and  just sheer scale  all right boys all right yeah boys epic  time  one of the hardest parts about that  whole trip was just as its remoteness  and how far it was from civilization  something goes wrong we're about 12  hours away in the best case scenario  from any hospital or serious health  the landscape up in the high arctic was  just it was breathtaking standing at the  top of the line just  soaking it all in it's  it's a pretty rad feeling  one thing that's amazing about mountain  biking is the fact that you can take it  anywhere you can climb mountains with it  you can descend mountains with it you  can travel long distances with it and  you can stuff it in a box and fly it  around the world  [Music]  to go up to the high arctic 400 miles  south of the north pole and ride my  bikes it's a pretty amazing thing to do  and check that off the bucket list for  sure  hey everybody my name is drew beebe and  i'm here in my terrible home studio that  i've made during quarantine  and i wanted to tell you about our new  podcast called great big story it's got  more surprising and delightful stories  just like this one so head over to apple  podcast to spotify wherever you get your  favorite podcasts and download great big  story
 

